# Hand-authored prose documents with their own formatting conventions (the docs/*.md
# "############ / # ENTITY / Name" delimiter blocks, specific emphasis style) — Prettier's
# markdown formatter rewrites these in ways that change visual structure, not just whitespace.
# Discovered when `prettier --write .` (run while chasing an unrelated CI formatting failure)
# reformatted nearly every file in docs/ as a side effect. Code and config still get formatted
# normally; only prose content is excluded here.
docs/**/*.md
CLAUDE.md
README.md
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Playwright's own output. Git already ignores it (apps/e2e/.gitignore), so CI never sees it on a
# clean checkout — but locally it is written by every browser run and then fails `format`, which
# turns "run the whole gate before pushing" into a step that reliably reports a problem nobody
# introduced. A generated directory has no formatting to check.
apps/e2e/test-results/
apps/e2e/playwright-report/
